323	595,1165,1380,1830	823. American Linden, in flower.	A twig of American Linden with a broad, toothed, heart-shaped leaf; from its axil hangs a long narrow bract whose stalk carries a small cluster of flowers and buds.
324	150,1150,518,1498	324. Magnified cross-section of a flower-bud.	A plan of the Linden bud cut across: five outer sepals, five petals, five clusters of small circles for the stamens with a scale in each, and the five-celled ovary at the centre.
325	160,1545,490,1905	325. A tuft of stamens with the petal-like scale.	One cluster of Linden stamens, their filaments joined at the base and fanning out to oblong anthers, with a broad petal-like scale standing in the middle.
326	1422,1545,1518,1820	326. Pistil.	The Linden pistil: a rounded, downy ovary tapering into a long slender style with a small stigma at the tip.
327	1372,1245,1512,1445	327. Fruit cut in two.	The small, round, woody Linden fruit on its stalk, cut across the top to show the single seed inside.
